\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces (a)~AUC@10 ranks for 6 methods on 5 classification datasets (Friedman $\chi ^2{=}13.80$, $p{=}0.017$, Kendall's $W{=}0.55$). (b)~AUC@10 heatmap: darker cells indicate higher AUC. NSGA-II occupies a mid-table position (avg.\ rank 3.2), reflecting its multi-objective nature. The CD diagram confirms all pairwise comparisons are non-significant at $\alpha {=}0.05$ (Nemenyi CD $\approx 3.4$ ranks for $k{=}6, N{=}5$). AUC@20 shows the same pattern (Appendix~\ref {app:stats}).}}{8}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cd_heatmap}{{1}{8}{(a)~AUC@10 ranks for 6 methods on 5 classification datasets (Friedman $\chi ^2{=}13.80$, $p{=}0.017$, Kendall's $W{=}0.55$). (b)~AUC@10 heatmap: darker cells indicate higher AUC. NSGA-II occupies a mid-table position (avg.\ rank 3.2), reflecting its multi-objective nature. The CD diagram confirms all pairwise comparisons are non-significant at $\alpha {=}0.05$ (Nemenyi CD $\approx 3.4$ ranks for $k{=}6, N{=}5$). AUC@20 shows the same pattern (Appendix~\ref {app:stats})}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:cd_heatmap@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][7][]8}{}{}{}}
